<h2>Professional Experience</h2>

<h3>Lead Web Developer | BookiesMasters (Freelance Project)</h3>
<p><em>Remote | [Date Start] – Present</em></p>
<p>Lead developer for a high-traffic commercial football prediction web application, delivering real-time data and premium content.</p>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Full Stack Architecture:</strong> Architected and built a scalable web application using <strong>Next.js</strong> and <strong>React</strong>, coupled with a <strong>Node.js</strong> backend, ensuring high performance and SEO visibility.</li>
    <li><strong>Responsive UI/UX Design:</strong> Designed and implemented reusable, responsive UI components (e.g., Fixture Cards, Live Score Boards) that provide a seamless user experience across all devices.</li>
    <li><strong>Real-time Data Integration:</strong> Integrated REST APIs to fetch and process real-time football data (livescores, odds, predictions), implementing efficient polling strategies to ensure up-to-the-second accuracy.</li>
    <li><strong>Payment Gateway Integration:</strong> Successfully integrated <strong>Intasend</strong> and <strong>Paystack</strong> for secure payments, enabling users to purchase VIP tips via complex flows including <strong>M-Pesa</strong> mobile money transactions.</li>
    <li><strong>Performance Optimization:</strong> Leveraged Next.js Server-Side Rendering (SSR) and Incremental Static Regeneration (ISR) to achieve fast load times and optimized Core Web Vitals.</li>
    <li><strong>Feature Development:</strong> Continuously enhanced the application with features like "Match Conditions" (weather/travel analysis) and "Live Odds" animations, directly improving user engagement.</li>
    <li><strong>Code Quality & Version Control:</strong> Maintained a clean codebase using <strong>Git</strong> for version control, managing feature branches and releases effectively.</li>
    <li><strong>Deployment & CD:</strong> Managed cloud deployments and continuous delivery pipelines via <strong>Vercel</strong>, ensuring high availability and rapid iteration.</li>
</ul>

